You can read your `N`  `FluxPointsDataset` objects as you wish. 
Then when plotting need to loop over those objects and the `axs`. For example:

```
LC_Swift_XRT = FluxPointsDataset.read("LC.ecsv",name='Swift_XRT_HE')
LC_Swift_XRT2 = FluxPointsDataset.read("LC.ecsv",name='Swift_XRT_HE2')

fpds = [LC_Swift_XRT, LC_Swift_XRT2]
fig,axs = plt.subplots(nrows=2, ncols=1, figsize=(10,5), dpi=120, sharex=True)
for ax, fpd in zip(axs, fpds):
    fpd.data.plot(ax=ax,
                  sed_type='eflux')
```

